  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0187\" consists of five tables: Farm, Crop, Plot, Planting_record, and Harvest_record.\nThe Farm table represents the information about the farms. It has columns for Address, Contact_information, Farm_ID (as the primary key), and Owner_name and Owner_type.\nThe Crop table contains information about the crops. It has columns for Crop_ID (as the primary key), Crop_name, Growth_cycle, Suitable_climate_conditions, and Suitable_soil_type.\nThe Plot table holds information about the plots. It has columns for Area, Current_status, Farm_ID (with a foreign key reference to the Farm table), Plot_ID (as the primary key), and Soil_type.\nThe Planting_record table records the details of crop planting. It has columns for Crop_ID (with a foreign key reference to the Crop table), Expected_harvest_time, Operator, Planting_quantity, Planting_time, and Plot_ID (with a foreign key reference to the Plot table). The primary key for this table is a combination of Plot_ID and Crop_ID along with Planting_time.\nLastly, the Harvest_record table records the details of crop harvest. It has columns for Crop_ID (with a foreign key reference to the Crop table), Harvest_quantity, Harvest_time, Operator, and Plot_ID (with a foreign key reference to the Plot table). The primary key for this table is a combination of Plot_ID and Crop_ID along with Harvest_time. All these tables are interconnected, ensuring referential integrity and maintaining the relationships between the data.",
  "gold_question": "Business requirements description for a Farmland Management Information System: The system needs to manage multiple farms, with each farm recording farm ID, farm owner name, owner type (company or individual), owner contact information, and address. Each farm can have multiple plots of land. Each plot has a plot ID, area, soil type, crops, and current status (such as \"sowing\", \"growing\", \"harvesting\", etc.). Each crop has an ID, name, growth cycle, suitable soil type, and suitable climate conditions. For each planting operation, the system needs to record plot ID, crop, planting time, expected harvest time, planting quantity, and operator. For each harvesting operation, the system needs to record plot ID, crop, harvest time, harvest quantity, and operator.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0187.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0187\nCREATE TABLE `farm` (\n  `farm_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`farm_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `crop` (\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `growth_cycle` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `suitable_climate_conditions` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `suitable_soil_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`crop_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `plot` (\n  `plot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `area` float NOT NULL,\n  `current_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `soil_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `farm_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`plot_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `plot_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`farm_id`) REFERENCES `farm` (`farm_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `planting_record` (\n  `plot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `planting_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `expected_harvest_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operator` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `planting_quantity` float NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`plot_id`, `crop_id`, `planting_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `planting_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crop` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `planting_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`plot_id`) REFERENCES `plot` (`plot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `harvest_record` (\n  `plot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `harvest_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `operator` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `harvest_quantity` float NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`plot_id`, `crop_id`, `harvest_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `harvest_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crop` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `harvest_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`plot_id`) REFERENCES `plot` (`plot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
